      "rationale":"The point register maps signals but does not establish valve states, so it cannot explain the cause of P-R dropping.","status": "supported","sourceIds":["da0260c0-7d49-43e8-b074-da2a14c7d59c#1"],"claimIds":[],"counterfactual":"If the point register established valve states, it could explain whether a specific valve was open or closed.","competingExplanation": "The inability of the register to show valve states does not prove no change occurred; an undocumented action is possible. The competing explanation is that an unrecorded physical change happened.","evidenceGap": "No evidence from other sources (logs, drawings) showing actual valve positions at 10:00."
