  ],"decision":{"summary":"The focal event was a transient loss of instrument air pressure at RHOB receiving header H-R between 10:00 and 10:03 AM. The evidence supports that the area directory, point register, and work package documentation do not establish valve positions or specific actions taken during this window. Multiple supported conditions (normal upstream pressure P-U stable at 6.9 bar) suggest the interruption was likely due to an unrecorded change in service routing or distribution system rather than equipment failure at the receiving end. However, no direct evidence confirms whether a specific valve move or routing change occurred; thus, this remains an unresolved gap.","evidenceUsed":["b678a928-a8d2-472d-bc03-2e1a3dc411e6#1","eaee59fe-70f4-4876-a21d-780814412078#1","da0260c0-7d49-43e8-b074-da2a14c7d59c#1","24ec1587-92e9-4320-82c2-30368d834f1d#1"],"unknowns":["Whether an unrecorded valve move or routing change occurred at 10:00 AM.","What specific field operation caused P-R to drop while P-U remained stable."],"alternatives":["An upstream supply issue (e.g., compressor trip, distribution leak) rather than a local valve move.","A documented but misinterpreted alarm condition that did not reflect actual pressure loss."],"confidence":0.65},"evidenceRequests":[
    "requestId\":\"req-1\",\"sourceId\":\"eaee59fe-70f4-4876-a21d-780814412078#1\",\"claimRef\":\"finding-1hfd1r1\",\"question\":\"Does the work package cover or any attached field execution record show a specific time when a valve was moved or routing changed?","rationale\":\"This would confirm whether an unrecorded action occurred.","evidenceGap\":\"No evidence of actual field operation log showing a specific time when a valve was moved."
  ]}
